==================================================================================================
0. HOW TO READ THIS FILE
==================================================================================================

NOTATION   This file reuses the local declarative notation of Artifact 067, with the CHECK line
           Artifact 069 added. It is an implementation choice, not COOLBOY12 architecture, and
           establishes no repository-wide schema language (SC-071-B). No parser exists for it.

           ELEMENT <name>        a structural element of a materialized Record
           LAYER                 ENVELOPE (universal, RMS §4) or FAMILY (Registry-model-owned)
           REQUIRED              yes | no
           CARDINALITY           exactly-one | …
           CONSTRAINT            what a conforming value must satisfy
           CHECK                 how the constraint is checked, as Artifact 069 defines it:
                                   NATIVE    decidable from the Record alone
                                   EXTERNAL  needs evidence outside the Record; the line names
                                             who supplies it, and this contract does not claim
                                             it proven
                                   STATIC    a property of this contract, checked by reading it
           BASIS                 where the element or rule comes from:
                                   SOURCE FACT            stated by a governing source
                                   REQUIRED SYNTHESIS     forced by several source facts together
                                   REPOSITORY CONVENTION  a choice of Artifact 067 or 069, reused
                                   071 CHOICE             a representation decision of this file
                                 REPOSITORY CONVENTION is the one addition to the notation, a
                                 071 choice.
           REJECT                a value that does not conform, with the rule it breaks and its
                                 CHECK

STATUS     This contract describes the structure a materialized SUBTYPE-DEFINITION Record must
           satisfy. It is not a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION Record, not a SCHEMA-DEFINITION Record, not a
           CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY, not the schema of any classified domain Record, and not
           canonical data. It is an authored source outside canon/** (Roadmap §0.8; CONFLICT-F).
           Concrete SUBTYPE-DEFINITION Records are committed only through the Mutation
           Coordinator (row 152) after G-CANON-R (070 SD-13). Where this contract differs from
           the Master Blueprint, the Record Model System, the Roadmap, or Artifact 070, those
           sources are right and this contract is wrong.

SPEC       Artifact 070 — docs/registry/subtype_definition.md — is the semantic contract this file
           encodes, consumed unchanged (H: 070). This file encodes only the structural
           consequences of the obligations 070 establishes (070 §25). Artifacts 067 and 069 are
           precedents for notation and representation conventions only: no semantics is taken
           from the MODEL-DEFINITION or KIND-DEFINITION families, and neither row is a
           dependency of row 071.

==================================================================================================
1. RECORD SHAPE
==================================================================================================

SUBTYPE-DEFINITION RECORD
├── ENVELOPE  partition · kind · object_id · slug · provenance · registry_ref · sot_class
└── FAMILY    owning_model · parent_kind · specialization · definition
              ├── owning_model, parent_kind and specialization together carry the ONE
              │   specialization context
              └── definition carries its governed meaning

Artifact 071 defines exactly these eleven elements: the universal seven-field envelope (RMS §4)
and four family elements. It defines no other element.

That is the scope boundary of this contract, not a closure over everything a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION
Record may later carry. Rows 108–110 keep their authority to establish Registry-owned evolution,
versioning, supersession and deprecation representation (§5 VERSIONABILITY; 070 VS-070-2). The
envelope, by contrast, stays exactly seven fields: no downstream Registry representation becomes
an eighth universal field (RMS §4; P-05).

One context, three carriers. 070 requires exactly one specialization within exactly one declared
parent Kind of exactly one owning Record Model (070 SD-1, RF-070-1), and fixes no count of
structural carriers. This contract carries that one context in three elements: owning_model gives
the owning model's scope, parent_kind names the parent Kind within it, and specialization names
the specialization within that Kind. No element alone is the context; together they are exactly
one. A specialization name is read only within its parent Kind (070 §8).

Three roles, never merged. The envelope element kind names this Record's own Kind — always
SUBTYPE-DEFINITION. parent_kind names the declared Kind the specialization belongs to — for
example LINEAGE. specialization names the specialization — for example HOUSE. They are different
elements in different roles. The specialization is never a Kind (070 SD-3), and neither the
parent Kind nor the specialization is ever this Record's kind (070 §19).

Not the classified Record. A domain Record carries a specialization as kind + <kind>_type
(Blueprint §13.6). This contract is the structure of the Registry Record that governs what the
specialization means, not of the classified domain Record: it defines no <kind>_type field and no
classification value for any model (P-04; 070 SD-11).

==================================================================================================
2. ENVELOPE — the universal seven (RMS §4; Artifact 033)
==================================================================================================

Types, defaults, nullability and serialization of the envelope fields are not established by the
governing sources (Artifact 033) and are not stated here.

ELEMENT     partition
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  R — the Registry partition
CHECK       NATIVE
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION is a Registry Record (RMS §10, §10.1; 070 §5,
            RS-070-1)
REJECT      W, E, P, V or I — a Record of an owning model, such as one Lineage, is never a
            SUBTYPE-DEFINITION                                    (SD-4; RF-070-5)  NATIVE

ELEMENT     kind
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  identifies the declared Registry Kind SUBTYPE-DEFINITION (Kind 3 of RMS §10.1) — this
            Record's own Kind, never its parent Kind and never its specialization. The constraint
            is symbolic. No two-character Registry Kind code is established; none is minted here
            (SC-071-C).
CHECK       NATIVE against the symbolic Kind; against a code only once the Registry's codes are
            bound by their own rows (row 117; Artifact 060 writes the code schematically as <kind>)
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §10.1; Artifact 064 §10
REJECT      KIND-DEFINITION — the parent Kind's own definition is another Registry Kind
                                                                  (SD-8)            NATIVE
            CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY — a governed value set is another Registry Kind
                                                                  (SD-9)            NATIVE
            any other Registry Kind                                                 NATIVE
            the parent Kind (for example LINEAGE) or the specialization (for example HOUSE)
            placed here                                           (070 §19)         NATIVE
            any invented code (for example SD) presented as established             NATIVE

ELEMENT     object_id
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the object identity component under the universal identity grammar. It is this
            Record's identity — not the parent Kind, not the specialization or its classification
            value, not a Kind code (070 RS-070-1).
CHECK       NATIVE
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4, §5; 070 RS-070-1

ELEMENT     slug
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  decoration only; never identity, never the basis of resolution
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value
            STATIC — this contract gives slug no identity or resolution role
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §5; Artifact 033

ELEMENT     provenance
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it: this Record's own provenance capture.
            Provenance meaning is not defined here, and the provenance of a Record classified by
            the specialization — how one Visual asset was produced, for example — is never
            carried here (070 SD-7, §12).
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

ELEMENT     registry_ref
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the universal envelope field, unchanged. This contract attaches no referent,
            self-reference convention, bootstrap target or resolution meaning to it, and it
            carries neither the parent Kind nor the specialization.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033 leaves its referent unresolved; Blueprint §9.4:
            reference resolution is not Registry work

ELEMENT     sot_class
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it. No value is fixed here; Artifact 071's own
            manifest SoT and Canon are not Record-level values and are not copied into it.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

==================================================================================================
3. FAMILY — SUBTYPE-DEFINITION content (Registry-model-owned; not envelope fields)
==================================================================================================

Each family element is required and exactly-one. None has a default value, and none may be left
empty: a Record without one does not conform, and this contract supplies no value for it (071
CHOICE). Types and serialization of the family elements are not established by the governing
sources and are not stated here; this contract fixes structure, not an encoding.

ELEMENT     owning_model
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  one value from the closed set   W | E | P | R | V | I
              W  World       E  Epistemic   P  Production
              R  Registry    V  Visual      I  Issue
            The sovereign Record Model whose own Kind taxonomy declares parent_kind — the owning
            Record Model of 070 SD-1. It is the model part of the parent-Kind scope: it scopes
            parent_kind and asserts nothing else about the model. It is not a subject of its own,
            not a separate declared-Model reference relation (070 RF-070-4), not a
            MODEL-DEFINITION reference, and not the owner of this Record, which is the
            Registry's (partition R; 070 SD-7). It confers no ownership.
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, membership of the closed set
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 070 SD-1 (exactly one owning Record Model), RF-070-1 (the parent
            a declared Kind of its owning model); RMS §2; RMS §6.1. Carrying model scope as its
            own element follows 069's subject_model (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). The element NAME,
            taken from 070's "owning Record Model", is a 071 CHOICE.
REJECT      no value — a parent Kind of no model                  (SD-1)            NATIVE
            two or more values — ambiguous scope                  (SD-1)            NATIVE
            a value outside the set, e.g. S "Simulation" claimed as a seventh model
                                                                  (RMS §2)          NATIVE
            a Record identifier or a runtime object — neither is in the set
                                                                  (RF-070-5, RF-070-6)
                                                                                    NATIVE

ELEMENT     parent_kind
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  names one Kind exactly as the Kind taxonomy of the model in owning_model declares it —
            for example LINEAGE under W, VISUAL-ASSET under V. The name is read only within
            owning_model. The value names the Kind itself — never a Record of that Kind, never the
            Kind's KIND-DEFINITION Record, never a two-character kind code (SC-071-C), and never a
            specialization.
            Declared status. The named Kind must be a declared Kind of owning_model, with that
            status established by the owning model's own Kind architecture (070 SD-2, RF-070-1;
            Artifact 063 §7 row 3, §8). A SUBTYPE-DEFINITION neither declares nor admits it
            (070 SD-2).
            Form. parent_kind is a declaration reference to the declared Kind, not an R → R
            reference to the parent's KIND-DEFINITION Record (070 RF-070-3; Artifact 063 §8.3).
            Why this form, and not both, is set out in §5 REPRESENTATION.
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; the value is not shaped as a Record identifier
            under the universal grammar (RMS §5); the pair is not (W, WSV).
            EXTERNAL — declared status, and that the Kind is owning_model's. The proof comes from
            the owning model's Kind architecture (Artifact 063 SC-063-H). This contract does not
            define or prove that evidence. Downstream legality validation may enforce this
            requirement under its own contract; row 112 independently enforces its narrower
            domain-instance reference prohibition. An undetermined parent is not legal (Artifact
            063 RB-6; 070 RF-070-1).
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 070 SD-1, SD-2, RF-070-1, RF-070-3; Artifact 063 §6, §8.3,
            SC-063-G (the form of a declaration reference is fixed by the applicable family
            contract or schema). The declaration form and naming the Kind by its declared name
            follow 069's subject_kind (REPOSITORY CONVENTION); choosing that form under RF-070-3
            is a 071 CHOICE (§5 REPRESENTATION). The element NAME, taken from 070's "parent
            Kind", is a 071 CHOICE.
REJECT      no value — a specialization with no parent Kind       (SD-1; RF-070-1)  NATIVE
            two or more Kinds, e.g. LINEAGE and ORGANIZATION together, defining HOUSE within both
                                                                  (SD-1)            NATIVE
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-LI-…-<slug> (a domain instance)
                                                                  (RF-070-5)        NATIVE
            a KIND-DEFINITION Record's identifier, R-<kind>-…     (RF-070-3)        NATIVE
            WSV under W — the WSV singleton is not a Kind (Roadmap PART III)        NATIVE
            a name owning_model has not declared — a candidate; a rejected candidate such as
            VISUAL-DERIVATIVE under V; a specialization such as GENERATED-IMAGE under V, which is
            a subtype and so never a parent                       (SD-2, SD-3)      EXTERNAL
            a declared name under the wrong model, e.g. LINEAGE under V
                                                                  (SD-1)            EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     specialization
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  names the one specialization whose meaning this Record governs — a classification
            within parent_kind (070 §6, §8): for example HOUSE within (W, LINEAGE), or
            GENERATED-IMAGE within (V, VISUAL-ASSET). The name is read only within the pair
            (owning_model, parent_kind); the three values together are the specialization
            context. The value names the specialization itself — never a Kind or kind code
            (070 SD-3), never a Record or Record identifier (RF-070-5), never a runtime object
            (RF-070-6).
            Scoped, not global. The same name under two parent Kinds names two contexts, carried
            by two Records (070 §8). This contract requires no uniqueness of a name across parent
            Kinds and creates no global subtype namespace, enum or taxonomy (070 SD-10).
            Name form. The name is written as the governing sources or the owning model's design
            work name the specialization (070 §14). This contract fixes no identifier grammar,
            case rule or spelling for it, and maps it to no classification value a domain Record
            carries (SC-071-M).
            Not a reference. specialization names this Record's own subject. It refers to no
            declaration and no Record: there is no declared-subtype target, and a specialization
            is reached through its SUBTYPE-DEFINITION (070 RF-070-2; Artifact 063 §7).
            Not a vocabulary link. This contract neither requires nor forbids that the name also
            appear as a value of a CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY; that relation is not established
            (SC-071-G).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; the value is not shaped as a Record identifier
            under the universal grammar (RMS §5); it differs, as written, from parent_kind.
            EXTERNAL — that the value names a specialization of parent_kind which the governing
            sources or the owning model's design work establish (070 §14; SC-071-H), and that it
            is no Kind name, kind code or runtime object of any model: Kind rosters and codes are
            the owning models' (Artifact 063 §8.3, §9). This contract does not prove it.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 070 SD-1, SD-3, SD-10, RF-070-2, RF-070-5, RF-070-6, §8, §14.
            The examples are SOURCE FACTS: HOUSE within LINEAGE (Blueprint §9.4, §13.6) and the
            Visual production forms (RMS §11.1). The identifier-shape check follows 069
            (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). Carrying the specialization as its own named element, the
            element NAME and the name form are 071 CHOICES.
REJECT      no value                                              (SD-1)            NATIVE
            two or more specializations, e.g. GENERATED-IMAGE and PHOTOGRAPH together
                                                                  (SD-1)            NATIVE
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-LI-…-<slug> or V-<kind>-…-<slug> (a domain instance)
                                                                  (RF-070-5)        NATIVE
            a Registry Record identifier, R-<kind>-…, such as a CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY Record's —
            the specialization is this Record's own subject, not a reference to another Record
                                                                  (RF-070-2)        NATIVE
            the parent Kind itself, e.g. LINEAGE within (W, LINEAGE)
                                                                  (SD-3)            NATIVE
            a Kind name or kind code, e.g. LI, World's code for LINEAGE
                                                                  (SD-3)            EXTERNAL
            VISUAL-REFERENCE within (V, VISUAL-ASSET) — a field, provenance or reference
            structure, not a production form                      (RMS §11.1)       EXTERNAL
            a running generator, service or validator named as the specialization
                                                                  (RF-070-6)        EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     definition
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the governed meaning of the specialization: what is true of it, as a specialization of
            what is true of every Record of parent_kind (070 §6; Artifact 062 L3). Non-empty. Its
            internal form is not prescribed by this contract. It carries none of: parent_kind's
            own meaning, which is its KIND-DEFINITION's (SD-8); a value set or vocabulary (SD-9);
            any Record of parent_kind, any value one carries, or what is true of one (SD-4); the
            classification field, its schema or its validation (SD-11); parent_kind's place in a
            taxonomy or its admission (SD-2); the owning model's domain semantics of the Records
            that use the subtype — for a Visual asset, its actual provenance and Visual's
            provenance meaning included (SD-7; 070 §12); anything that redefines or overrides
            what is true of every Record of parent_kind (SD-6).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, non-empty.
            EXTERNAL — the content limits are semantic and not decidable from structure; they are
            judged against 070, and this contract does not claim them proven.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 070 §6, SD-4, SD-6 to SD-9, SD-11; RMS §6.1 (governs; never
            instantiates); Blueprint §9.4 Subtype semantics row. The single carrier, the element
            NAME and the non-empty rule follow Artifacts 067 and 069 (REPOSITORY CONVENTION).
REJECT      executable behaviour, a factory, or a registration, approval or admission action
                                                                  (SD-4, SD-12)     EXTERNAL
            a domain instance, domain state, derived output or runtime object as the source of
            meaning — e.g. one VISUAL-ASSET Record cited as what GENERATED-IMAGE means
                                                  (RF-070-5, RF-070-6; 062 D-3, D-5) EXTERNAL
            the classification field's name, type or value set    (SD-9, SD-11)     EXTERNAL
            a statement that overrides what holds of every Record of parent_kind
                                                                  (SD-6)            EXTERNAL

==================================================================================================
4. STRUCTURAL PROHIBITIONS
==================================================================================================

P-01A Artifact 071 introduces no element beyond the eleven of §1. Prohibited here as universal
      semantics (P-06), as ownership, admission or sovereignty (P-03), as runtime structure
      (070 RF-070-6) or as another family's content (P-07): status, tier, lifecycle_state,
      canonical, history, relationship_record, owner, owns_records, admitted,
      admission_rationale, taxonomy_member, kind_code, subtype_code, implementation, service,
      worker, session, process, handler, factory, generator.
P-01B Artifact 071 introduces no version, revision, latest-version, supersession, replacement,
      deprecation, retirement, effective-date, migration, compatibility or retention element or
      mechanism, and no lifecycle or state machine. That representation is deferred to rows
      108–110: neither defined nor permanently prohibited here (070 VS-070-2). Whatever those
      rows establish stays Registry-owned, is not an envelope field (P-05) and is not a
      universal semantic shared by W, E, P, V or I (P-06).
P-02  No generic reference list, and no reference the obligations of 070 do not require:
      references, refs, dependencies, related_records, definition_refs, kind_refs,
      kind_definition_ref, model_ref, schema_ref, subtype_refs, vocabulary_ref,
      controlled_vocabulary_ref, vocabulary_id, vocabulary_value_ref. A structural reference
      encodes only an obligation 070 establishes — here, the parent-Kind scope — or
      representation a named downstream owner establishes; an admissible target category alone
      authorizes nothing (070 RF-070-4; Artifact 063 RB-5).
P-03  No element names, carries or implies: ownership of parent_kind or of its Records; a
      decision on which Records carry which classification; admission or approval of the parent
      Kind or of the specialization; membership in a taxonomy; or sovereignty. The owning model
      keeps its taxonomy, its Records and their domain semantics; the Registry owns this Record
      and governs the specialization's meaning (070 SD-7). A legal reference transfers no ownership,
      mutation authority, semantic authority, admission, canonicality or source-of-truth class
      (070 RF-070-8).
P-04  Not the schema of any domain Record. No element carries the classification field of any
      model — its name (for example lineage_type), type, cardinality, serialization or value set
      — or the fields, requiredness or order of parent_kind's Records; those belong to the owning
      model's field architecture and schema rows (070 SD-11; SC-071-K).
P-05  No envelope field added, removed or renamed. The family elements are not envelope fields,
      and no <kind>_type, subtype, kind_type, classification, parent_kind or specialization field
      enters the envelope (RMS §4; 070 §19).
P-06  None of RMS §4's prohibited universal semantics: Record base, Relationship Record, History
      Record, lifecycle, canonicality, Kind taxonomy, identity composition, state model, semantic
      schema. For this family that means no universal subtype superclass; no global subtype
      taxonomy, namespace or identifier grammar; no forced enum across Kinds; no universal
      <kind>_type; no Relationship Record joining a specialization to its parent; and no History
      Record for its versions (070 §19, SD-10).
P-07  Not another family's contract: not KIND-DEFINITION (070 SD-8) and not
      CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY (070 SD-9) — no value-set element, no vocabulary-membership element,
      no mandatory vocabulary link — and not MODEL-, FIELD-, SCHEMA- or
      RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION. No element embeds another family's definitions, and nothing
      here pre-builds row 350's VISUAL-ASSET subtype vocabulary.
P-08  No element records an LS-1 pairing, a Kind specification artifact or a lockstep partner.
      LS-1 is not a reference and creates no commit atomicity here (070 §20; SC-071-A).
P-09  No dependency element. The L3 semantic dependency on the parent Kind holds because the
      sources establish it (Blueprint §9.4; Artifact 062 §5). parent_kind is a declaration
      reference, which is not by itself a semantic dependency (Artifact 062 D-9; 070 RF-070-9),
      and a dependency is not a reference field (Artifact 062 §9). Concrete dependency rules are
      row 111's.
P-10  No element represents how a specialization comes to exist or is added, proposed,
      approved, admitted or declared. Row 459 owns the extensibility contract — "each through
      its own ceremony, never through a generic abstraction" — and Artifact 065 owns governance
      (070 SD-12; SC-071-H).

REJECTED DEDUCTIONS — each with the check that rejects it and where

 1  a subtype is a Kind                          NATIVE, EXTERNAL, STATIC  §2 kind; §3; P-01A
 2  a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION is a domain instance    NATIVE                    §2 partition, kind
 3  a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION is a KIND-DEFINITION    NATIVE, STATIC            §2 kind; P-07
 4  a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION is a CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY
                                                 NATIVE, STATIC            §2 kind; P-07
 5  a specialization with no parent Kind         NATIVE                    §3 parent_kind
 6  a parent Kind belonging to no model          NATIVE                    §3 owning_model
 7  a parent model outside W, E, P, R, V, I      NATIVE                    §3 owning_model
 8  a domain Record identifier as the subject    NATIVE                    §3 specialization
 9  a runtime object as subject or authority     NATIVE, EXTERNAL, STATIC  §3; P-01A
10  a global subtype namespace                   STATIC                    §3; P-06
11  a global subtype enum                        STATIC                    P-06
12  <kind>_type added to the universal envelope  NATIVE, STATIC            §2; P-05
13  a vocabulary reference made mandatory        STATIC                    P-02, P-07
14  a reference read as a semantic dependency    STATIC                    P-09; §5
15  resolution read as legality                  STATIC                    §5 RESOLUTION
16  a legal reference read as ownership transfer STATIC                    P-03; §5
17  versionable read as licence for a version field
                                                 STATIC                    P-01B; §5
18  LS-1 read as a subtype lockstep pair         STATIC                    P-08; SC-071-A
19  Canon or CD read as licence to write canon   STATIC                    §5; SC-071-E
20  row 071 used to pre-build row 350's vocabulary
                                                 STATIC                    P-07; §5
21  row 071 used to invent row 459's ceremony    STATIC                    P-10

==================================================================================================
5. BOUNDARIES
==================================================================================================

REPRESENTATION  070 RF-070-3 leaves to 071 which form carries the parent-Kind scope: naming the
                declared Kind, or an R → R reference to the parent's KIND-DEFINITION Record.
                This contract uses the declaration form — owning_model and parent_kind — and not
                both, since a second relation would be an invented one (070 RF-070-4). The
                choice is a 071 CHOICE, not a Blueprint or RMS fact. Its grounds:
                (1) it is the form Artifact 069 uses for a declared-Kind subject (REPOSITORY
                    CONVENTION);
                (2) it needs no KIND-DEFINITION Record to exist first. The R → R form would make
                    every SUBTYPE-DEFINITION wait for its parent's KIND-DEFINITION, an order the
                    Roadmap does not state: row 350, built on 071, does not list row 345, the V
                    Kind-Definition set, in its H (PART IX X-05, consumer before provider).
                    Whether row 350 carries SUBTYPE-DEFINITION Records is itself not established
                    (SC-071-G);
                (3) the R → R form needs a Registry Record identifier — where a target is a
                    Record, its handle is a resolvable ID (Artifact 063 §11) — and no Registry
                    Kind code is bound yet (row 117; SC-071-C).
                The form creates no semantic authority, dependency or ownership: a declared Kind
                named as a target is not semantic authority for the definition that names it,
                and naming it is not by itself a semantic dependency (Artifact 063 §7 row 3;
                Artifact 062 D-9). The specialization is the Record's own subject and is carried
                by name, not by reference (070 RF-070-2).

RESOLUTION      A conforming Record carries the baseline Record identity that later
                Registry-definition resolution requires (§2): partition, kind and object_id.
                Artifact 071 does not by itself establish the complete id+version resolution
                representation: rows 108–110 retain authority over Registry evolution and version
                representation, and row 115 owns consumer resolution — "consumer resolves by
                id+version". Resolution never relies on slug, which is decoration only.
                owning_model, parent_kind and specialization name the semantic context and do not
                thereby become this Record's identity. This contract implements no resolver,
                lookup, index, cache, storage, fallback, version-selection or classification-value
                lookup, and does not say how a consumer finds the definition of a given
                specialization; row 114 owns Registry create/resolve/version operations.
                Resolution transfers nothing, and resolvable is not legal (Artifact 063 §11).
                (070 RS-070-1 to RS-070-5)

VERSIONABILITY  Nothing here prevents the Registry evolution and versioning model of rows 108–110
                from applying to a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION. Artifact 071 defines no version
                identifier, numbering scheme, pinning representation, supersession, replacement
                or deprecation representation, effective date, migration, retention or
                compatibility rule, or temporal lifecycle mechanism; those decisions stay with
                rows 108 (evolution), 109 (versioning, pinning) and 110 (supersession,
                deprecation). Nor does it say whether two Records may carry the same context —
                as versions of one definition, for example — or how such Records relate; that is
                theirs too. This contract is open to whatever Registry-owned representation those
                rows establish, provided it leaves the seven-field envelope unchanged and keeps
                within the Record Model boundaries (P-05, P-06); no World History Record is used
                or required (I-102). Versionable therefore means: Artifact 071 does not
                structurally obstruct the evolution and versioning architecture rows 108–110 own.
                Absence here is not a decision that a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION carries no version.
                (070 VS-070-1, VS-070-2)

REFERENCES      The one concrete reference this family carries is the parent-Kind scope: a
                declaration reference to a declared Kind of a declared Record Model — not an
                R → R reference to a KIND-DEFINITION Record, not an owned edge and not a
                Relationship Record (070 RF-070-1, RF-070-3; Artifact 063 §8.3; I-102). The
                specialization is no reference target: there is no declared-subtype category
                (070 RF-070-2; Artifact 063 §7; SC-071-J). No W/E/P/V/I domain instance, no domain
                state and no runtime instance is a target, a dependency or an authority. A
                reference transfers no ownership, admission or authority, is not by itself a
                semantic dependency, and is not legal because it resolves. (070 RF-070-1 to
                RF-070-9)

LAYER           A SUBTYPE-DEFINITION sits at L3, subtype semantics (Artifact 062 §4.3). No
                element takes meaning from L4 or L5, and this contract carries no dependency
                element (P-09). It carries exactly one parent Kind and no other Kind: whether
                subtype semantics may depend on a Kind other than their own is not established
                (SC-071-L).

VOCABULARY      No element carries a value set, a vocabulary reference or vocabulary membership.
                Whether every value of a vocabulary has a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION, whether one
                vocabulary serves one parent Kind, and how the two families connect are not
                established (SC-071-G). Row 350 builds the VISUAL-ASSET subtype vocabulary on
                rows 071 and 082 under its own row. Nothing here requires a vocabulary link, and
                nothing forbids one that a later source establishes.

CLASSIFICATION  Classified domain Records carry the specialization as kind + <kind>_type —
                "There is one classification field, not two" (Blueprint §13.6). That field is the
                owning model's: its name, type and value form are not stated here (SC-071-K), and
                this contract maps no specialization name to a classification value (SC-071-M).

LS-1            Row 071 carries LS: LS-1 and Why: LS-1. This contract is not a Kind
                specification and not a KIND-DEFINITION; 070 ↔ 071 is not a Kind ↔
                KIND-DEFINITION pair, and no subtype pair is created. The Registry's own pairs
                stay 064 ↔ 075; the KIND-DEFINITION of the Kind SUBTYPE-DEFINITION is one of row
                075's fourteen and conforms to 069, not to this file (SC-071-A).

MATERIALIZATION This file is an authored source. A SUBTYPE-DEFINITION Record conforming to it is
                committed to canon/registry/** only through the Mutation Coordinator after
                G-CANON-R (Roadmap §0.8, PART X; 070 SD-13). No Roadmap row names
                SUBTYPE-DEFINITION Records as its output: Registry content extends by ordinary
                Registry change (Blueprint §9.4), and whether row 350 carries such Records is not
                established (SC-071-G). Nothing here authors or commits any Record, and
                Canon: canonical-about-meaning and CD: yes license no write (SC-071-E).

DOWNSTREAM      Row 071's → names 347, the CANONICAL-VISUAL-SPECIFICATION schema, whose H is 346
                only. This contract imposes nothing on row 347 and assigns it no subtype or
                vocabulary responsibility. Row 350 lists 071 in its H, with 348 and 082, and
                consumes this contract under its own row; nothing here builds it or widens its
                Val (SC-071-I). A downstream artifact uses this contract only as its own H and
                Val allow.

