7. SOURCE CONDITIONS
==================================================================================================

SC-071-A  LS-1. Row 071 carries LS: LS-1 and Why: LS-1. Roadmap PART III defines LS-1 as every
          Kind spec ↔ its Registry KIND-DEFINITION, an atomic pair. This contract is neither a
          Kind specification nor a KIND-DEFINITION, 070 ↔ 071 is not such a pair, and no source
          states which pair, if any, row 071's label names (070 SC-070-D). The Registry's own
          pairs stay 064 ↔ 075 (AD-LS1-R-BOOTSTRAP). No subtype ↔ SUBTYPE-DEFINITION pair,
          070 ↔ 071 pair, lockstep class, commit atomicity, dependency or reference is invented.
          Recorded, not resolved; ROADMAP ISSUE, non-blocking.
SC-071-B  No schema language is established. The notation of §0 is Artifact 067's local choice
          with Artifact 069's CHECK line, reused; REPOSITORY CONVENTION as a BASIS label is a 071
          choice. It is no repository-wide language.
SC-071-C  No two-character Registry Kind code is established, and kind codes outside World are
          not frozen (Artifact 063 §9). The envelope kind is constrained symbolically,
          parent_kind is named rather than coded, and no code is minted for a specialization.
          Identity binding is row 117's.
SC-071-D  Req: RR-16 is carried exactly; its text is unavailable (GAP-C) and is not invented.
SC-071-E  Row 071 carries T: schema · Canon: canonical-about-meaning · CD: yes on a docs/** path.
          Artifact 003's general convention gives a docs/** specification Canon: n/a; whether it
          reaches a schema contract is not stated. The metadata is preserved exactly; this file
          is not a Registry Record, and CD: yes licenses nothing (070 SC-070-I; SC-069-E).
          Recorded, not resolved.
SC-071-F  Declared status has no single proof mechanism across the six models (Artifact 063
          SC-063-H). parent_kind's declared status is therefore an EXTERNAL check whose proof is
          the owning model's; this contract does not prove it and does not define how it is
          proved. Recorded, not resolved; non-blocking.
SC-071-G  SUBTYPE-DEFINITION and CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY (070 SC-070-E). No source fixes the
          cardinality, identity or reference relation between subtype definitions and
          vocabulary values. Row 350 builds the VISUAL-ASSET subtype vocabulary on rows 071 and
          082; whether it also carries SUBTYPE-DEFINITION Records is not established. This
          contract carries no vocabulary element, requires no vocabulary link and forbids none a
          later source establishes. Recorded; non-blocking.
SC-071-H  How a specialization comes to exist and is added (070 SC-070-F). Registry content
          extends by ordinary Registry change (Blueprint §9.4); row 459 owns how a visual
          subtype is added; Artifact 065 owns governance. No admission, declaration or extension
          element is defined (P-10). Recorded; non-blocking.
SC-071-I  Row 071's → names 347, but row 347 carries H: 346 only, while row 350 carries
          H: 348,071,082 and is not named by row 071's → (070 SC-070-G). → 347 is preserved;
          this contract assigns row 347 nothing and pre-builds nothing for row 350. ROADMAP
          ISSUE, non-blocking.
SC-071-J  No declared-subtype reference category (070 SC-070-H; Artifact 063 §7). Settled by the
          frozen contract: specialization names this Record's own subject and is not a
          reference.
SC-071-K  The classification field outside World (070 SC-070-L). No current source names the
          field that carries the VISUAL-ASSET classification. This contract needs none: it names
          no domain field for any model (P-04). Non-blocking.
SC-071-L  Dependence on a Kind other than its own (070 SC-070-M; Artifact 062 §6). Not
          established. This contract carries exactly one parent Kind, no other Kind and no
          dependency element. Non-blocking.
SC-071-M  Specialization name vs classification value. The Blueprint names the specialization
          HOUSE within LINEAGE (§9.4), while a classified Record carries lineage_type: house
          (§13.6); RMS §11.1 names the production forms GENERATED-IMAGE and the others. No source
          states whether the name a SUBTYPE-DEFINITION carries and the value a classified Record
          carries are one token, or how case and spelling map between them; how a consumer
          finds the definition of a specialization is likewise not defined (070 RS-070-5). This
          contract carries the specialization by name, fixes no identifier grammar, case rule or
          spelling, and maps no name to a value. The value form is the owning model's field
          architecture's (SC-071-K) and any value set the vocabulary's (SC-071-G). Recorded, not
          resolved; non-blocking for the structure.
SC-071-N  Roadmap §2.3, Hinge artifacts, lists "071 KIND-DEFINITION", but row 071 is the
          SUBTYPE-DEFINITION schema and KIND-DEFINITION is rows 068 and 069; other entries of
          that list also differ from the manifest (it names "133 Mutation Coordinator", which is
          row 152). Row 071's manifest entry states this artifact's ID, name and path (Artifact
          003, fields 1–3). The §2.3 entry is not read as making this file a KIND-DEFINITION
          artifact or a hinge, and nothing here acts on it. Recorded, not resolved; ROADMAP
          ISSUE, non-blocking.

